Description: libcamera: software_isp: Fix black level handling in CPU ISP
 Backport of upstream libcamera commit 7d650a23d1685610fc209c7d050027b793ef03a0.
 The CPU ISP applied the black level after white balance instead of before,
 and used a single (green) black level for all three channels. Rewritten by
 hand for 0.7.0: upstream depends on Vector::clamp(), which does not exist
 here, so .max(0.0f).min(x) is used instead, and the code lives in DebayerCpu
 rather than the not-yet-existing DebayerCpuThread.
Origin: upstream, https://git.libcamera.org/libcamera/libcamera.git/commit/?id=7d650a23d1685610fc209c7d050027b793ef03a0
Author: Milan Zamazal <mzamazal@redhat.com>
